  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisector Market Study West Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Western Ukraine faces many (economic) challenges and is so far lagging compared to the rest of Ukraine. However, this part of Ukraine also offers many new opportunities in different sectors. These are the agro-food, horticulture, biomass, industry and machine building, construction materials, chemical industry, and metal works sectors. Considering the expertise of the Netherlands in these sectors, the Netherlands can contribute to the development of the western regions and, at the same time, gain from the established business links. The envisioned expanded involvement of Dutch companies in this part of Ukraine can contribute to increased productivity of the local sectors, more jobs and ultimately to the overall private sector development of the region. However, to fully understand and contribute to the private sector development of West Ukraine, the essential private sector development (PSD) challenges for the seven regions or so-called oblasts of West Ukraine have to be identified. Furthermore, the identified opportunities for Dutch companies in Western Ukraine should motivate Dutch businesses to come to this region.</narrative>
  </description>
